    "description": "The file provided is a PDF file of the PhD thesis completed by Jane Wasley in 2004. The thesis research was based on field work conducted in the Windmill Islands region (based at Casey station), during two consecutive summer seasons: 1998/99 and 1999/00.  \n\nBelow is a list of the main areas of research covered by the thesis; providing chapter-level broad subject areas, with reference to relevant publications and metadata IDs where relevant.  \n\n1. Chapter 1 - Introduction/literature review (published in Robinson et al 2003) \nMetadata ID: Not applicable. \n\n2. Chapter 2 - General Methods\nMetadata ID: Not applicable - but content may be relevant to metadata records related to other data chapters below.\n\n3. Chapter 3 - Transects (published in Wasley et al 2012)\nMetadata ID: ASAC_1087_Transects_1999-00\n\n4. Chapter 4 - water and nutrient enrichment experiment (published in Wasley et al 2006a) \nMetadata ID: ASAC_1087_Water_NutrientExpt\n\n5. Chapter 5 - moss species desiccation tolerance (Wasley et al 2006b)\nMetadata ID: ASAC_1087-Desiccation",
